{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced","id":1416164,"title":"What happens when a hunter with true faith is embraced?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-30T14:39:58-07:00","id":1416164,"title":"What happens when a hunter with true faith is embraced?","content":"This is V20 we're dealing with here, but would be curious about other editions.<br /> <br /> So, this actually happened last game session where the characters were fighting some hunters. One of the players decided to embrace one of the dying hunters that had true faith. I gave him a shot at just dying peacefully by rolling his true faith and he completely botched it.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking to start with, for at least the time being, he loses a point of faith for this happening but retains the rest unless he were to do something that might be in conflict with his faith's beliefs. So when the group opens the trunk of the car they stuffed him into, he could still brandish his holy symbol at them and attempt to flee as long he doesn't frenzy from hunger. I'm probably going to go with this but was just curious how others have dealt with this in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:28:55-07:00","id":1416169,"title":"","content":"They become NYTEBLADE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_Wo0SmtbaQU\" data-code=\"_Wo0SmtbaQU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_Wo0SmtbaQU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;So, Nyteblade fights vampires.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But the Order still hunts him, because he's a vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;YES!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:42:06-07:00","id":1416172,"title":"","content":"Bringing such a being into the fold is no easy task. Depending on how smart the hunter is, he simply may bides his time and turn on the group. But it easily could go in the opposite direction and he could be the most debauched of them all after a short period. Forsaken by his god an all that. Or he sees it as a test and he has to sacrifice his humanity to safe humanity (which in the long run will and badly for him).<br /> <br /> I would decide depending on what the group does in his training. But with the few extras, under no circumstances he would drink human blood (even to a point where he might die or frenzy), he will not kill humans only other monster. Of course he sees himself now as one and is in ennui half the time in the beginning.<br /> <br /> Oh, depending on the organization your troupe is in they are in hell themselves. What were they thinking embracing someone with true faith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:47:27-07:00","id":1416175,"title":"","content":"Oh, I should've mentioned they're a nomadic Sabbat pack undercover in a city the Cam only has a loose grasp on, so random chaos is right up their alley. Another thing I'm pondering is how should true faith interact with the Vaulderie? I haven't quite decided how I want to deal with that, should they manage to force him to drink from the cup.<br /> <br /> In my head I'm kind of hoping he gets away, just to create more trouble. He could potentially try to make contact with his church or get picked up by the local Cam. He might blow their cover if the Cam gets their hands on him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T22:50:16-07:00","id":1416209,"title":"","content":"As a ST would probably lean in the same direction but I would get my players a fighting chance to manipulate and influence said hunter to become a member of the pack. But I would make it hard, like really hard and with dire consequences if they fail. If they fail and don't kill the hunter-vampire banishment from the city will be one of the more harmless option. If he flees his sole mission is to kill those who denied him heaven.<br /> <br /> As Sabbat one of the angles the could use, would be the antediluvians. &quot;Yeah, we're bad, but wait what will happen if the 10000 year old blood gods wake up and fight it out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","user":"Meldok","date":".  Adding the last paragraph 10-01-2020, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T06:56:53-07:00","id":1416250,"title":"","content":"Well, since the reason the Embrace took in the first place was a botched Faith, i would say goes to the deep end, hard.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's the Lord's will i be remade as a monster!!!&quot; crazed epiphany, hunter goes full-on Lancea Sanctum (from Requiem) style raving lunatic zealot, imho.<br /> <br /> The hunter keeps the True Faith, but it twists in peculiar, beast-fueled ways. Giving it any Noddist lore, further <i>validating </i>a biblical worldview, only serves to makes things worse, possibly leading to recovery of any lost Faith, now taken in strange directions (along with maybe inadvertently learning a path even without appropriate teachers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-01-2020, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T11:13:46-07:00","id":1416309,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of thinking I might go with a bit of both. It should be hard for them to keep him and he'll try to get away, but it is possible for him to get indoctrinated. Maybe even willpower expenditure can counter the Vaulderie, at least for a little while. If they do manage to indoctrinate him, though, he'll go all in on the Noddist lore and being a monster to fight Gehenna. I strongly suspect they're probably just going to want to interrogate him and destroy him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T12:44:29-07:00","id":1416321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced#post1416164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking to start with, for at least the time being, he loses a point of faith for this happening but retains the rest unless he were to do something that might be in conflict with his faith's beliefs. So when the group opens the trunk of the car they stuffed him into, he could still brandish his holy symbol at them and attempt to flee as long he doesn't frenzy from hunger. I'm probably going to go with this but was just curious how others have dealt with this in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little suggestion?<br /> When the hunter awakens inside the trunk of the car they stuffed him into, his Faith is still whole and mostly the same.<br /> When they open it, he still brandishes his holy symbol at them as he always could, making them flinch and retreat.<br /> But also himself. He feels the hurt, the fear, <b><i>the Beast that is also him</i></b> recoiling from the symbol as he calls upon the Lord still.<br /> <b>Then</b>, the reality sinks in of what he has become, that point of Faith drops and he stops resisting, for a time at least...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416309#post1416309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of thinking I might go with a bit of both. It should be hard for them to keep him and he'll try to get away, but it is possible for him to get indoctrinated. Maybe even willpower expenditure can counter the Vaulderie, at least for a little while. If they do manage to indoctrinate him, though, he'll go all in on the Noddist lore and being a monster to fight Gehenna. I strongly suspect they're probably just going to want to interrogate him and destroy him</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say he'll be confused and divided, seeing his condition as punishment for some subtle failure or an ordeal he must thread through for the sake of rendemption. If interrogated by the pack, he might come to see it as an opportunity for that, willingly giving them what info he has, to trick the servants of darkness into an ambush, even if he must martyr himself for the sake of the Lord's design.<br /> <br /> If his old colleagues fail to eliminate the monsters, well, that's where things go pear-shaped and he might go into the darker places of the soul to make sense of his Faith and persisting connection to the Lord, as he sees it.<br /> <br /> Either way, i'd say he could be surprisingly open to conversation and learning, both for the sake of intel for initial plans of infiltration/betrayal/martyrdom and later on to try and make sense of his ever (d)evolving undead condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-01-2020, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:10:19-07:00","id":1416327,"title":"","content":"If I were ST, the hunter would attempt to flee as soon as possible. Reveal as much damaging information he's learned during that time as he could. And then walk out into the sun to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> I don't see how anyone with actual True Faith would want to continue existing as a vampire. Non-True Faith hunters could very well let their fear of death overwhelm their hatred of vampires. But I think those with True Faith wouldn't tolerate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:16:43-07:00","id":1416328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced#post1416164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is V20 we're dealing with here, but would be curious about other editions.<br /> <br /> So, this actually happened last game session where the characters were fighting some hunters. One of the players decided to embrace one of the dying hunters that had true faith. I gave him a shot at just dying peacefully by rolling his true faith and he completely botched it.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking to start with, for at least the time being, he loses a point of faith for this happening but retains the rest unless he were to do something that might be in conflict with his faith's beliefs. So when the group opens the trunk of the car they stuffed him into, he could still brandish his holy symbol at them and attempt to flee as long he doesn't frenzy from hunger. I'm probably going to go with this but was just curious how others have dealt with this in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your solution. His unlife would be dedicated to regaining his True Faith and then igniting that Faith in others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:19:49-07:00","id":1416329,"title":"","content":"don't know if it's a good example but he's the only one I can think of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Christof_Romuald\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Christof_Romuald</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:59:45-07:00","id":1416337,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of him feeding misinformation to the pack. I think it should at least be a possibility he sees it as a test of his faith, depending on how things play out. He should try to get away if at all possible as his first step. There's the possibility of only feeding off animal blood or the occasional murderer, so he doesn't have to commit suicide if he believes this is all just god testing him. There definitely would be a period of confusion before he arrives at that conclusion.<br /> <br /> Wasn't Christof's faith already in decline at the start of Redemption? You could put points into it, but you had to go out of your way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T03:38:08-07:00","id":1416458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416327#post1416327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were ST, the hunter would attempt to flee as soon as possible. Reveal as much damaging information he's learned during that time as he could. And then walk out into the sun to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> I don't see how anyone with actual True Faith would want to continue existing as a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, given that Abrahamic religions treat suicide largely as sin and a sure way to hell, I think especially people with True Faith would refrain from it.<br /> <br /> He was put there either by God to become a monster to fight the monster. Or by the devil to tempt him. <br /> <br /> But as long as he has his True Faith, he will not completely succumb to darkness and the beast. Sure things will get harder over time, but as long as he can retain it, he will fight the good fight. What ever that means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T12:37:22-07:00","id":1416508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416458#post1416458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, given that Abrahamic religions treat suicide largely as sin and a sure way to hell, I think especially people with True Faith would refrain from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely disagree with this entire logic. Vampires are monsters. They're abominations in the eyes of God. Destroying them is not the same moral act as killing people. Therefore, a vampire destroying itself is not the same thing as a mortal committing suicide. Destroying vampires is always a moral good. I can't think that any religious teachings would ever accept the idea that being a vampire wouldn't be an absolute metaphysical evil that must be destroyed in all cases.<br /> <br /> Suicide is a sin because it's considered to be a rejection of God's gift of life and the full time that is allotted to them. Obviously that does not apply to a vampire who has already been murdered by the person who turned them. A vampire's mere existence is an inherent evil. A vampire that destroys itself isn't committing a sin against God. It's undoing the terrible desecration against life that the state of undead is and returning the person's soul to the bosom of God. It is an affirmation of the value of life against the blasphemous nature of the undead and restoration of God's order on earth.<br /> <br /> I believe someone with True Faith would instinctively know this and accept what must be done. Higher levels of True Faith would most assuredly cause the vampire to destroy itself. Although I could see very low levels be subject to possible temptation or fear and ignore the calling. But that should be the exception of what would happen. And as a result, the character is likely in danger of losing the True Faith merit over time. And I don't think it would take long for that to happen.<br /> <br /> I do think people without True Faith - who detest vampires and while they are alive would think they are better off destroyed if they are ever turned by them - could easily fall into the trap you're laying out for them, especially with the Beast doing whatever it can to survive. Without the blessing of True Faith, it would take a lot of Willpower to do what's needed.<br /> <br /> I understand there are many players who interpret True Faith differently, and there are vampire characters with the True Faith merit. (As well as the idea that destroying vampires is always a moral good.) I've never liked that and have always rejected it in my games. I think it's doing a disservice to the True Faith concept to do otherwise. I also believe any game of Gothic Horror needs some level of moral absolutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T13:50:29-07:00","id":1416525,"title":"","content":"I think either is a view someone in that situation could take. They might consider destroying themself and ridding the world of a monster something that would be good or they could see it as anathema to their religion and it being a test from god like Job. It's subjective and up to individual interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T14:29:16-07:00","id":1416535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416508#post1416508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I completely disagree with this entire logic. Vampires are monsters. They're abominations in the eyes of God. Destroying them is not the same moral act as killing people. Therefore, a vampire destroying itself is not the same thing as a mortal committing suicide. Destroying vampires is always a moral good. I can't think that any religious teachings would ever accept the idea that being a vampire wouldn't be an absolute metaphysical evil that must be destroyed in all cases.<br /> <br /> Suicide is a sin because it's considered to be a rejection of God's gift of life and the full time that is allotted to them. Obviously that does not apply to a vampire who has already been murdered by the person who turned them. A vampire's mere existence is an inherent evil. A vampire that destroys itself isn't committing a sin against God. It's undoing the terrible desecration against life that the state of undead is and returning the person's soul to the bosom of God. It is an affirmation of the value of life against the blasphemous nature of the undead and restoration of God's order on earth.<br /> <br /> I believe someone with True Faith would instinctively know this and accept what must be done. Higher levels of True Faith would most assuredly cause the vampire to destroy itself. Although I could see very low levels be subject to possible temptation or fear and ignore the calling. But that should be the exception of what would happen. And as a result, the character is likely in danger of losing the True Faith merit over time. And I don't think it would take long for that to happen.<br /> <br /> I do think people without True Faith - who detest vampires and while they are alive would think they are better off destroyed if they are ever turned by them - could easily fall into the trap you're laying out for them, especially with the Beast doing whatever it can to survive. Without the blessing of True Faith, it would take a lot of Willpower to do what's needed.<br /> <br /> I understand there are many players who interpret True Faith differently, and there are vampire characters with the True Faith merit. (As well as the idea that destroying vampires is always a moral good.) I've never liked that and have always rejected it in my games. I think it's doing a disservice to the True Faith concept to do otherwise. I also believe any game of Gothic Horror needs some level of moral absolutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it depends on what you see as the basic tenets of True Faith. And also whether True Faith is only found among the Abrahamic religions. I\u2019ve never played in a campaign that dealt extensively with the concept, but I find it interesting. Could my Wiccan character have True Faith in Gaia? What would happen if she was Embraced by a Gangrel? Would she follow the Garou philosophy and start hunting other vampires? Or would she instead choose the Wiccan motto of Do No Harm and try to coexist with her new Kindred siblings? What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T15:27:53-07:00","id":1416543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416535#post1416535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it depends on what you see as the basic tenets of True Faith. And also whether True Faith is only found among the Abrahamic religions. I\u2019ve never played in a campaign that dealt extensively with the concept, but I find it interesting. Could my Wiccan character have True Faith in Gaia? What would happen if she was Embraced by a Gangrel? Would she follow the Garou philosophy and start hunting other vampires? Or would she instead choose the Wiccan motto of Do No Harm and try to coexist with her new Kindred siblings? What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya it's possible for other religions to produce individuals with true faith, but they were less frequent. The V20<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />A Tome of Secrets briefly touches on this in the faith section and gives Druidism and even faith in love as possibilities. It's still an extreme and fanatical level of belief and rare for anyone to have it, though. It's entirely subjective about whether they'd go hunting vampires or consider them a part of nature, so it could go either way depending on the individuals own beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T20:12:41-07:00","id":1416566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416327#post1416327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how anyone with actual True Faith would want to continue existing as a vampire. Non-True Faith hunters could very well let their fear of death overwhelm their hatred of vampires. But I think those with True Faith wouldn't tolerate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, when I'm running games attempts to embrace people with True Faith just fail outright, the vampiric curse is unable to find purchase on the soul to draw it back from death and inflict unliving damnation on it. Vampires can still <i>develop</i> True Faith postmortem, but it's not something that can be carried over from life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T20:38:39-07:00","id":1416567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416566#post1416566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, when I'm running games attempts to embrace people with True Faith just fail outright, the vampiric curse is unable to find purchase on the soul to draw it back from death and inflict unliving damnation on it. Vampires can still <i>develop</i> True Faith postmortem, but it's not something that can be carried over from life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about doing that, but said screw it on the spot, werewolves have to botch a roll for the embrace to succeed and ran with that, surprisingly he botched the roll, so here we are <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T20:57:00-07:00","id":1416568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416566#post1416566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, when I'm running games attempts to embrace people with True Faith just fail outright, the vampiric curse is unable to find purchase on the soul to draw it back from death and inflict unliving damnation on it. Vampires can still <i>develop</i> True Faith postmortem, but it's not something that can be carried over from life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do pretty much the same, their faith is rewarded by a peaceful death and an honored place amongst the faithful in heaven.<br /> <br /> But in this case, probably kill the one who embraced them and meet the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T22:02:35-07:00","id":1416569,"title":"","content":"I think Sullivan Dane being Embraced would be interesting, especially as a contrast to Nathaniel Borduff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T22:23:39-07:00","id":1416572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416569#post1416569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Sullivan Dane being Embraced would be interesting, especially as a contrast to Nathaniel Borduff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense if he were active into modern nights, Hell, it's been nearly 30 years since he first showed up in the lore. He'd be pretty old if something hadn't slowed/stopped his aging by now. I think he was probably the first hunter I knew by name as a kid. There's a lot of potential there for him, with damned near any clan being the one that perpetrated the act as a form of revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T22:29:16-07:00","id":1416573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416572#post1416572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would make sense if he were active into modern nights, Hell, it's been nearly 30 years since he first showed up in the lore. He'd be pretty old if something hadn't slowed/stopped his aging by now. I think he was probably the first hunter I knew by name as a kid. There's a lot of potential there for him, with damned near any clan being the one that perpetrated the act as a form of revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my campaign, I established that Sullivan Dane started to awaken during one of his latter missions and is now close to becoming a Choir mage but the experience has the potential to destroy his faith (learning some if not all of his miracles are just his own will).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T22:59:47-07:00","id":1416577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416543#post1416543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ya it's possible for other religions to produce individuals with true faith, but they were less frequent. The V20<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />A Tome of Secrets briefly touches on this in the faith section and gives Druidism and even faith in love as possibilities. It's still an extreme and fanatical level of belief and rare for anyone to have it, though. It's entirely subjective about whether they'd go hunting vampires or consider them a part of nature, so it could go either way depending on the individuals own beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faith in love would be awesome \ud83e\udd70.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T23:01:21-07:00","id":1416578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416573#post1416573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my campaign, I established that Sullivan Dane started to awaken during one of his latter missions and is now close to becoming a Choir mage but the experience has the potential to destroy his faith (learning some if not all of his miracles are just his own will).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who is Sullivan Dane and how is he different than Nathaniel Bordruff?<br /> <br /> Nvm. I just looked him up. He does seem like an interesting contrast to Nathaniel Bordruff. I think there\u2019s a really good chance he\u2019s joined the Society of Saint Leopold by now, plus maybe he\u2019s like a professor at Georgetown in his mundane life (Georgetown is a Jesuit school). What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-03-2020, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T23:11:28-07:00","id":1416580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416578#post1416578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is Sullivan Dane and how is he different than Nathaniel Bordruff?<br /> <br /> Nvm. I just looked him up. He does seem like an interesting contrast to Nathaniel Bordruff. I think there\u2019s a really good chance he\u2019s joined the Society of Saint Leopold by now, plus maybe he\u2019s like a professor at Georgetown in his mundane life (Georgetown is a Jesuit school). What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think he was the OG Society of Leopold Hunter.<br /> <br /> It's just that he was an independent Jesuit hunter before being recruited, which is probably embarrassing to the SOL.<br /> <br /> I don't think he'd approve of teaming up with the US government, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T23:16:04-07:00","id":1416584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416580#post1416580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think he was the OG Society of Leopold Hunter.<br /> <br /> It's just that he was an independent Jesuit hunter before being recruited, which is probably embarrassing to the SOL.<br /> <br /> I don't think he'd approve of teaming up with the US government, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. That makes sense. What do you think of the Georgetown connection? (Even hunters need legit jobs as a cover or a source of income.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T23:20:24-07:00","id":1416585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416584#post1416584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. That makes sense. What do you think of the Georgetown connection? (Even hunters need legit jobs as a cover or a source of income.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a good retirement for him as any. I actually think I had him teaching there BEFORE he became a Hunter and discovered Kindred existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T23:51:26-07:00","id":1416589,"title":"","content":"Cool. Thanks.<br /> <br /> One more quick question. Somewhere I read about a hunter group called the Order of the Broken Branch with ties to Georgetown. Maybe Sullivan Dane could be connected to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T01:38:44-07:00","id":1416596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416535#post1416535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it depends on what you see as the basic tenets of True Faith. And also whether True Faith is only found among the Abrahamic religions. I\u2019ve never played in a campaign that dealt extensively with the concept, but I find it interesting. Could my Wiccan character have True Faith in Gaia? What would happen if she was Embraced by a Gangrel? Would she follow the Garou philosophy and start hunting other vampires? Or would she instead choose the Wiccan motto of Do No Harm and try to coexist with her new Kindred siblings? What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to think of what the True Faith merit is trying to emulate, and how the various world religions are depicted in folklore, legend, and pop culture. To me, True Faith is reserved for the Abrahamic religions (the one True Faith for the one True God) although I'd be willing to consider its use by Buddhist characters or even possibly Hindus. There are certainly stories of Buddhists encountering supernatural evil yet dispelling them similar to stories in Christianity, Judaism, and Islam. So I'd be open to players convincing me about the karmic religions, although I'd need to reframe the flavor text appropriately. However, for the various pagan religions, I think any &quot;magical&quot; powers of their devotees are best emulated by Sorcery Paths. Wiccans wouldn't get True Faith, but some of them might actually get their magic spells to be real. Certainly anyone from an authentic magical tradition like the historical (or fictional WoD version) Cult of Isis would have appropriate Sorcery Paths to reflect what they were supposed to have done.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'd ever allow True Faith in Gaia, although Gaia is objectively real in some sense in the WoD. I think of True Faith as being reserved for those faiths that normally don't get cool WoD powers. Technically some of the Abrahamic faiths adherents could get Theurgy powers through Solomonic magical practices, but those are not mainstream and typically looked upon suspiciously. In contrast, the Gaian faction has the Garou and all their powers, plus kinfolk who might have Gnosis and other things. So no, they don't get True Faith when I run chronicles as an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T02:42:37-07:00","id":1416599,"title":"","content":"- He could receive revelations from god (or delusions) giving him a purpose as undead.<br /> <br /> -He could 'realise' how wrong it is to hunt vampires and try to save their souls<br /> -He could, if you were to use the pre-revised rules, avoid the consumption of human blood and travel the world slaking his thirst on vampires; His high consciensce and righteous conviction preventing the beast from gaining sway (Diablerie only became an auto-humanity loss during revised, and I've got many issues with it)<br /> -He could gracefully meet the sun or destroy himself with his own faith. Plot twist he becomes human again and all the players flip their shit.<br /> -He could twist his religious beliefs into something crazy and... then behave like a normal vampire (if somewhat Setite-inspired)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T04:22:53-07:00","id":1416604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416535#post1416535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it depends on what you see as the basic tenets of True Faith. And also whether True Faith is only found among the Abrahamic religions. I\u2019ve never played in a campaign that dealt extensively with the concept, but I find it interesting. Could my Wiccan character have True Faith in Gaia? What would happen if she was Embraced by a Gangrel? Would she follow the Garou philosophy and start hunting other vampires? Or would she instead choose the Wiccan motto of Do No Harm and try to coexist with her new Kindred siblings? What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes she could. Then her faith would not repell demons and vampires anymore but BSD and Wyrm spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T04:43:03-07:00","id":1416606,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a> thank you both for answering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T05:23:23-07:00","id":1416616,"title":"","content":"I notably had Sullivan Dane bitten by Helena in a game and it resulted in her burning inside from every point of blood inflicting aggravated damage. It killed Sullivan but it was a worthy death.<br /> <br /> The con module, Rusted Veins, did something similar except it was Modius who was killed. While technically an Elder, I feel like Sullivan was slumming it there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-03-2020, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T21:56:07-07:00","id":1416681,"title":"","content":"Well the player that embraced him made the mistake of opening the trunk he was in while the others were occupied. He very nearly got away and it took three of them to bring him down. He's sitting staked in a garage in the suburbs now, so it'll be awhile till I get to know what they want to do with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T23:09:44-07:00","id":1416687,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=MyWifeIsScary;n1416599]-<br /> -He could, if you were to use the pre-revised rules, avoid the consumption of human blood and travel the world slaking his thirst on vampires; His high consciensce and righteous conviction preventing the beast from gaining sway (Diablerie only became an auto-humanity loss during revised, and I've got many issues with it)<br /> /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Its in my copy of Vampire 2e so I'm curious where you get its a creation of revised. ON the other hand.. Diablere is a choice. Well sometime its a failed roll but mostly its a choice mechanically you can feed perfectly well on kindred even kill them without...eating their souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T00:40:07-07:00","id":1416693,"title":"","content":"I double checked. <br /> <br /> Yeah, in first and second edition you roll for murder when you commit diablerie. The emphasis is put on eating life-force rather than soul. <br /> In revised and V20 you automatically lose a dot of humanity (or path, if it is adverse to diablerie or murder in general) and you might roll conscience again if the person you murdered was nice. Honestly I think the people writing the rules fell for anti-diablerie propaganda (or they thought vampires should be more dark and hopeless than they already were and were aiming for personal rather than political horror, or something)<br /> <br /> With the V1/V2 rules, you can diablerie a lot without losing humanity if your rolls are good. <br /> Of course, it may just be better to stake a victim, drain it when you're hungry, and execute it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T02:10:10-07:00","id":1416701,"title":"","content":"it's that paradox of the humanity system where the people with the highest humanity and conscience get to do more violation and diablerie,<br /> and you had that hillarious thing where serial killers with high virtues would have to act remorseful everytime they succeeded on the roll, then 10 seconds later go back to their murder spree<br /> <br /> imo, Revised did the right thing by making diablerie auto humanity loss, that way the serial diablerists had to maintain humanity with xp points instead of conscience,<br /> <br /> another good thing Revised did right was suggest that at lower humanity ratings, conscience acted more like conviction from other paths,<br /> that way, on a successful roll, the serial killer would be making excuses or rationalizing their actions instead of crying<br /> <br /> still, Revised morality system was still a damn long way from being good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T10:01:21-07:00","id":1416737,"title":"","content":"Nah, disagree strongly; revised fucked up there. <br /> <br /> From my experience, if people auto-lose humanity, they stop diablerising at a certain point. Absolutely will-not eat when they're at 3 humanity or lower unless the storyteller fucks them over. Even if a 4th gen prostrated themselves before them they'd never do it at humanity 1 because it's not even a risk, it's a death sentence. The system utterly fails at getting serious sinners to devolve further. The end result is that serial diablerists end up moderating their intake They're not junkies, they're planners. If there was a roll, some form of gambling, you could still do it. But if the storyteller gets involved it feels like a shitty railroad; You diablerise at humanity 5, storyteller gives you a derangement, every time you see a torpor'd body you eat it even if it's no value to you. You don't so much as rollplay a downward spiral as much as you play the prelude of being a wight as you've just lost control over your character. So either you moderate or you have a heavy-handed road to hell that's no good to play with. <br /> <br /> Plus, y'know, I've made the whole case that 'Bad things are scarier when they're easy' because then you've got to worry about them happening to you. Make it so bad that it's &quot;Diablerie, just once and you'll never do it again&quot; doesn't scare me as much as 'You just ate Dave, congratulations; you're the tastiest Cainite in the city now.' <br /> <br /> Ultimately I see Conscience as 'Ego' since, well, it's a stat where you need more of it the worse you want to be. It doesn't make sense for it to be the nice-guy stat when nice people don't actually need it. Monsters need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T14:42:09-07:00","id":1416766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416701#post1416701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's that paradox of the humanity system where the people with the highest humanity and conscience get to do more violation and diablerie,<br /> and you had that hillarious thing where serial killers with high virtues would have to act remorseful everytime they succeeded on the roll, then 10 seconds later go back to their murder spree</div> </div> </div> </div>That was definitely a problem if you simply approached the issue solely mechanically. When I run games, I have honest conversations with their players. Do their PCs really think their action was wrong? More often than not, the answer is &quot;no.&quot; So they lose humanity (or certain Virtues) as a result. I only have them role when they can truly say their PCs regretted their actions.<br /> <br /> So what happens if they keep doing actions they regret? Well, that's a conversation with the player. Maybe it's just a series of bad luck where the character finds themselves forced in a bad situation. Hey, sometimes that happens. But I would expect to see some kind of reaction by the PC in an attempt to avoid whatever the root cause of that because a moral person would not want to be put into a situation that constantly comprises their moral integrity. If the PC doesn't have a real excuse, I may not wait until they finally role bad, but simply have them lose Humanity.<br /> <br /> I find players sometimes like to roleplay out their character's losing Humanity and going through a struggle as they do things they don't like, but feel they must. But typically there's a point when the player feels their PC has been handwringing long enough, and is happy to lose the Humanity. As long as the mechanics make sense, I'm happy to go through the rolls. But when a PCs actions clearly undermine their supposed traits, I don't mind lowering those traits by fiat to the level where their behavior is consistent with the character sheet.<br /> <br /> I find that most players don't want their characters to be morally obsessed over their actions. And my gaming group tends to be an honest bunch. So their PC's Humanity tends to reflect what they're actually doing. They tend to not want to spend time on their character's fall down the Humanity chart. They're fine with it being where they think it realistically belongs. I've had a few players who did like that to roleplay that fall because part of the fun for them was to start as a ordinary person and try to remain moral in this world.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible for a character to be a murderous psychopath compelled by urges to do evil, but have a high Conscience that it torments them and somehow retain their Humanity. Malkavian concepts in particular, might fit that. But there probably are some severe derangements that allows for that to paradox to happen. It's like in Psycho how Norman Bates believes he's not the actual killer, but it's his mother whom he tries to protect out of filial devotion while hating her actions at the same time. I do think these kind of character concepts are possible. However, I find that they really aren't PC concepts. They work best as NPC concepts. A player will quickly realize the limits of such a character in an ongoing chronicle (although they can be fun in one shot games), and then create a character that works better for a long term game.<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the conversations I have with players at the beginning of chronicles is where they feel their PC will go in terms of their Humanity versus where they are right now. Usually they'll start at a 6 or 7 (although some have been at 8!), but admit they see their PCs ultimately going to a 4 or even 3. I then ask them if they truly want to roleplay out the decline, or do they want me to simply lower their Humanity as they do more evil. Most either say that their humanity should just be lowered automatically until they hit 5 or 4, and then role. Or that they want to temporarily roleplay things out until there is a triggering event (which always comes), and then it can drop things to a lower level (like 4) where they'll roleplay things out again.<br /> <br /> It keeps things concentrated on being fun for them, but not forcing them to roleplay crises of conscience they don't actually feel is appropriate for the PC or fun for them to play in game.<br /> <br /> Dishonest or troublesome players would still object and claim I'm being unfair. But my game group is pretty reliable at unanimously deciding we need to remove those kind of players from our group. This system seems to work well for our game group because we all want the same kind of game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:09:18-07:00","id":1416769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416737#post1416737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, disagree strongly; revised fucked up there.<br /> <br /> From my experience, if people auto-lose humanity, they stop diablerising at a certain point. Absolutely will-not eat when they're at 3 humanity or lower unless the storyteller fucks them over. Even if a 4th gen prostrated themselves before them they'd never do it at humanity 1 because it's not even a risk, it's a death sentence. The system utterly fails at getting serious sinners to devolve further. The end result is that serial diablerists end up moderating their intake They're not junkies, they're planners. If there was a roll, some form of gambling, you could still do it. But if the storyteller gets involved it feels like a shitty railroad; You diablerise at humanity 5, storyteller gives you a derangement, every time you see a torpor'd body you eat it even if it's no value to you. You don't so much as rollplay a downward spiral as much as you play the prelude of being a wight as you've just lost control over your character. So either you moderate or you have a heavy-handed road to hell that's no good to play with.<br /> <br /> Plus, y'know, I've made the whole case that 'Bad things are scarier when they're easy' because then you've got to worry about them happening to you. Make it so bad that it's &quot;Diablerie, just once and you'll never do it again&quot; doesn't scare me as much as 'You just ate Dave, congratulations; you're the tastiest Cainite in the city now.'<br /> <br /> Ultimately I see Conscience as 'Ego' since, well, it's a stat where you need more of it the worse you want to be. It doesn't make sense for it to be the nice-guy stat when nice people don't actually need it. Monsters need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it depends, how often do you think vampires should hit wightdom?<br /> <br /> Because sometimes you just need vampires to go down forever and complete their story arc.<br /> <br /> Your players have to be on that train, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:23:03-07:00","id":1416772,"title":"","content":"In the Anarch Agata Starek Loresheet. The five dot benefit &quot;waives&quot; the autolost of the first dot of humanity for committing diablerie upon a Kindred of higher status. One of the &quot;joys of the revolution.&quot; I think that in a sect like the Sabbat, where diablerie is sanction either against non-Sabbat or through monomacy, a similar benefit should exist. I've contemplated a &quot;Sabbat Vampire&quot; loresheet, that would allow a Sabbat vampire a similar benefit. It wouldn't prevent the risk of being taken over, but it would allow the vampire, even at low humanity not to automatically lose that first dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:25:55-07:00","id":1416773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416766#post1416766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dishonest or troublesome players would still object and claim I'm being unfair. But my game group is pretty reliable at unanimously deciding we need to remove those kind of players from our group. This system seems to work well for our game group because we all want the same kind of game.</div> </div> </div> </div>never imagined this could work, but even if it does, I'm irrationally obsessed with the idea of fixing humanity and virtue mechanics once and for all,<br /> a thing that would satisfy both the chill players, the rule lawyers and those who cry &quot;unfair&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416737#post1416737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately I see Conscience as 'Ego' since, well, it's a stat where you need more of it the worse you want to be. It doesn't make sense for it to be the nice-guy stat when nice people don't actually need it. Monsters need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>the ego stat would be willpower, they stressed that pretty hard in kote<br /> conscience is def the good guy stat, since it's the stat you roll when your low humanity character wants to do something bad and you want to prevent them (STs can do that, I dont remember if that was in revised or V20)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From my experience, if people auto-lose humanity, they stop diablerising at a certain point. Absolutely will-not eat when they're at 3 humanity or lower unless the storyteller fucks them over. </div> </div> </div>I don't know if that's true, because I don't think I ever played on humanity,<br /> <br /> but I would think the diablerie addiction would solve that issue (again, I'm not sure if that was in revised or V20)<br /> there's also the Megalomania derangement. a vampire constantly violating their conscience would probably start developping derangements<br /> <br /> Revised also had an optional degeneration system (Chaining the Beast) where the vampire would develop minor versions of derangements as their humanity went low,<br /> the same book suggested making degeneration rolls only once per scene,<br /> I'd say at the end of the scene, the ST can just reward 1 or two xp points to the diablerist for acheiving their goal (diablerie), which they can spend on humanity...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-04-2020, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:58:22-07:00","id":1416779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruthven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416772#post1416772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Anarch Agata Starek Loresheet. The five dot benefit &quot;waives&quot; the autolost of the first dot of humanity for committing diablerie upon a Kindred of higher status. One of the &quot;joys of the revolution.&quot; I think that in a sect like the Sabbat, where diablerie is sanction either against non-Sabbat or through monomacy, a similar benefit should exist. I've contemplated a &quot;Sabbat Vampire&quot; loresheet, that would allow a Sabbat vampire a similar benefit. It wouldn't prevent the risk of being taken over, but it would allow the vampire, even at low humanity not to automatically lose that first dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loresheets are very good for justifying specialized rules that allow you to play the character you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T01:23:16-07:00","id":1416818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416769#post1416769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it depends, how often do you think vampires should hit wightdom?<br /> <br /> Because sometimes you just need vampires to go down forever and complete their story arc.<br /> <br /> Your players have to be on that train, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> So... you want to railroad them? <br /> <br /> I like chance. Characters should have both options when they're on the brink; damnation or redemption. 1 humanity should be a tight rope, not a stop-gap or a solid wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T01:31:46-07:00","id":1416820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1416164-what-happens-when-a-hunter-with-true-faith-is-embraced?p=1416818#post1416818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... you want to railroad them?<br /> <br /> I like chance. Characters should have both options when they're on the brink; damnation or redemption. 1 humanity should be a tight rope, not a stop-gap or a solid wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, quite the opposite, one of the things I've found is that if I want to see characters tortured and undergo the most ****ed up things imaginable then I don't do them to the Player Characters. I ask the players to come up with what sort of horrible things they can do to their characters and usually what they come up with is far more sick and twisted than anything I could do to them. Degenerating to wightdom and killing off their character due to diablerie or blood addiction or becoming an alien horror who must be killed are things that I have had players agree to because they like the idea of roleplaying it.<br /> <br /> With diablerie, the question is, &quot;Is this something that is so horrible it can and will drive Kindred to become mindless beasts.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, it was definitely one of the things that I put for, &quot;Can result in 0 Humanity&quot; but that happening is something I mostly put to the player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}